WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.837
Greater than ALL is stricter.

00:00:01.837 --> 00:00:06.672
The outer age must be greater than every age returned by the inner query.

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:10.232
A useful intuition is to compare with the maximum.

00:00:10.232 --> 00:00:15.997
To be greater than all returned ages, the outer value must exceed the largest one.

00:00:15.997 --> 00:00:20.112
Run the query and compare the row count with the ANY example.

00:00:20.112 --> 00:00:25.247
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:25.247 --> 00:00:31.692
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:31.692 --> 00:00:34.127
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:34.127 --> 00:00:40.722
In a real setting such as a hospital identifying patients above a benchmark or with no follow-up,

00:00:40.722 --> 00:00:46.957
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:46.957 --> 00:00:49.172
before discussing syntax.

00:00:49.172 --> 00:00:55.522
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
